      "text": "Hello! How's everything today?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 13.1,
      "end": 18.82,
      "text": "That's a great start. Once the root is a few centimetres long and a shoot appears at the top, it's ready for a pot."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 24.37,
      "end": 33.25,
      "text": "Honestly, probably not indoors. Trees from stones can take ten years or more and often need warmth we can't give them. But it makes a lovely leafy houseplant."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 38.35,
      "end": 44.35,
      "text": "Maybe sell it to him as a tree he grew himself. Kids usually love watching it shoot up, it can grow really fast."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 52.45,
      "end": 58.97,
      "text": "Medium to start, with good drainage. Leave the top half of the stone above the soil, and keep it in a bright spot."
